          text: 'End the day at a riverside restaurant with a plate of caldou (fish and tomato broth), grilled oysters harvested from the mangroves, and thieboudienne — the Casamance version uses palm oil and has a distinct southern flavour. The evening atmosphere in Ziguinchor is gentle and sociable — locals gather at tea stalls, children play in the streets, and occasionally a mbalax or traditional Diola drumming session starts up at one of the neighbourhood cultural spaces.',
          tip: 'Grilled mangrove oysters are a Casamance speciality found nowhere else in Senegal — try them at the small stalls near the river port. They cost 500-1,000 CFA per plate.',
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
  3: [
